{"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and lists no tracking domains.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Required-reason-APIs","type":"heading","text":"Required-reason APIs"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes"},{"text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp"},{"text":"), system boot time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime"},{"text":"), disk space","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace"},{"text":"), active keyboards","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards"},{"text":") and user defaults","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults"},{"text":"). The modules that come nearest:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Module"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What it calls"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Why none is a required-reason API","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"swift-system’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileDescriptor"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"open"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"read"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resize"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unlink"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileManager"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"createDirectory"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setAttributes"},{"text":" (the file protection class), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contentsOfDirectory"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isExcludedFromBackup"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It reads no file’s timestamps, size from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stat"},{"type":"text","text":", or the volume’s free space: a segment’s size is the offset "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"type":"text","text":" returns at its end, and the store bounds itself by the bytes it has written."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileManager.fileExists"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data.write(to:options:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileVersionStore"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProcessInfo.performExpiringActivity"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It reads and writes the version file’s contents, never its attributes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sysctlbyname"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hw.machine"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hw.model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProcessInfo.operatingSystemVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bundle.infoDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locale.current"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NWPathMonitor"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None is on the list; "},{"code":"Enricher.vendorIdentifier()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is declared as collected data below."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracker’s record timestamps ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A session’s inactivity is measured between records’ wall-clock timestamps, not from the system’s uptime.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Date.now","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wall-clock time, not boot time.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ContinuousClock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the default clock of "},{"code":"batch()","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift runtime’s clock, which isn’t on the list."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GRDB"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"GRDB ships a privacy manifest of its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"swift-crypto’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"SHA256","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is CryptoKit’s on Apple platforms","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Hashing is on no list. swift-crypto’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Crypto"},{"text":" bundles a privacy manifest of its own on Apple platforms, declaring no tracking, no required-reason API and no collected data.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every other module calls nothing near the list. Of the packages Traffluent depends on,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"swift-system’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Stat"},{"type":"text","text":" API ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FilePath.stat()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileDescriptor.stat()"},{"type":"text","text":") calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stat"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fstat"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lstat"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fstatat"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"statfs"},{"type":"text","text":". Traffluent calls none of it. If your app does, your manifest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declares the file timestamp or disk space reason it needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Collected-data","type":"heading","text":"Collected data"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every declaration below is ","type":"text"},{"code":"NS